\": {\"depth_0\": 2.222, \"depth_1\": 1.37, \"depth_2\": 1.006}, \"code_contamination\": {\"d0\": 0.004, \"d1\": 0.077, \"d2\": 0.116, \"d3\": 0.136}}, \"conclusion\": \"success\", \"notes\": \"## Comparison: temp_only τ=0.9 vs baseline nucleus p=0.95\\n\\n### 4-class classification (d0-d3)\\n| Metric | Baseline (nucleus p=0.95) | Temp09 (τ=0.9) | Δ |\\n|--------|--------------------------|-----------------|---|\\n| RF acc | 78.15% [76.9, 79.4] | 76.25% [74.9, 77.5] | -1.9pp |\\n| LR acc | 74.92% | 74.05% | -0.9pp |\\n| AUC 0v1 | 0.9975 | 0.9968 | -0.0007 |\\n| AUC 1v2 | 0.8607 | 0.8327 | -0.028 |\\n| AUC 2v3 | 0.8005 | 0.7928 | -0.008 |\\n\\n### 3-class classification (d1-d3 only)\\n| Metric | Baseline | Temp09 | Δ |\\n|--------|----------|--------|---|\\n| Full acc | 70.8% | 69.83% | -1.0pp |\\n| Filtered acc | — | 72.52% [70.6, 74.3] | — |\\n| Filtered d1v2 AUC | — | 0.8656 | — |\\n| Filtered d2v3 AUC | — | 0.8295 | — |\\n\\n### Feature importance (top-5, same ranking)\\n1. var_surprisal (0.178 vs 0.169)\\n2. p90_ppl (0.150 vs 0.158)\\n3. mean_ppl (0.114 vs 0.120)\\n4. mean_surprisal (0.089 vs 0.088)\\n5. p75_ppl (0.069 vs 0.067)\\n\\n### Code contamination\\n| Depth | Baseline | Temp09 | Δ |\\n|-------|----------|--------|---|\\n| d1 | 5.0% | 7.7% | +2.7pp |\\n| d2 | 9.0% | 11.6% | +2.6pp |\\n| d3 | 12.0% | 13.6% | +1.6pp |\\n\\n### Analysis\\n1. **Depth signal robust across decoding strategies**: temp_only τ=0.9 achieves 76.25% 4-class acc (vs 78.15% baseline), only 1.9pp lower — well within the hypothesis that depth signal is decoding-strategy-agnostic.\\n2. **Ordinal structure preserved**: AUC ordering 0v1 > 1v3 > 1v2 > 2v3 identical to baseline, confirming the difficulty gradient d0≫d1>d2>d3 is robust.\\n3. **d2 remains the weak link**: d2 recall (0.554 in 3-class) is the lowest, consistent with baseline — d2 is the hardest to distinguish from both d1 and d3.\\n4. **Feature importance stable**: Top-5 features identical between strategies with near-identical importance weights, suggesting the same statistical signatures carry depth information regardless of decoding method.\\n5. **Higher code contamination**: Temp09 shows 2-3pp higher code-like content across depths, possibly because temperature-only sampling without top-p truncation preserves more of the distribution tail including code patterns. The filtered 3-class acc (72.52%) mitigates this.\\n6. **Conclusion: SUCCESS** — 4-class acc 76.25% >> 40% threshold, d1v2 AUC 0.8327 >> 0.6 threshold. Hypothesis confirmed: temperature-only decoding preserves recursive depth signal.\", \"completed_at\": \"2026-05-14T16:42:54.633Z\"}, \"mvp_pipeline_pythia_002\": {\"status\": \"DONE\", \"retry_count\": 0, \"created_at\": \"2026-05-14T12:07:25.860Z\", \"updated_at\": \"2026-05-14T16:13:24.461Z\", \"spec\": {\"command\": \"bash scripts/run_pipeline.sh (Pythia-1.4B, 3x LoRA finetune + 3x generate)\", \"server\": \"gpu-6000pro-2\", \"gpu\": \"cuda:0\", \"pid\": 103739, \"log_path\": \"/root/autodl-tmp/recursive_gen_depth_est/logs/pipeline_pythia.log\", \"submitted_at\": \"2026-05-14T12:10:06.848Z\", \"submitted_via\": \"submit_training_job\", \"backend\": \"tmux\", \"account\": \"root\", \"data_path\": \"/root/autodl-tmp/recursive_gen_depth_est/data/depth_0.jsonl\", \"data_count\": 5000, \"model_name\": \"EleutherAI/pythia-1.4b\", \"model_path\": \"/root/autodl-tmp/models/pythia-1.4b/\", \"seed\": 42, \"hypothesis\": \"Pythia-1.4B (The Pile, 代码仅3.3%) 递归生成的文本具有可区分的统计模式，4-class acc > 40% 且 depth-1 vs depth-2 AUC > 0.6\", \"hyperparams\": {\"lora_r\": 16, \"lora_alpha\": 32, \"target_modules\": [\"query_key_value\"], \"epochs\": 3, \"lr\": \"2e-4\", \"batch_size\": 8, \"gradient_accumulation\": 2, \"max_seq_len\": 512, \"max_new_tokens\": 512, \"temperature\": 1, \"top_p\": 0.95}, \"checkpoint_path\": \"/root/autodl-tmp/recursive_gen_depth_est/checkpoints/lora_depth_{0,1,2}/\", \"wall_clock_seconds\": 6420, \"gpu_hours\": 1.78, \"pipeline_metrics\": {\"finetune_loss_d0\": 2.2411, \"f